  "status": "historical-reviewed",
  "captureMonth": "2011-11",
  "review": "The four November 2011 panoramas place the miniature beside the visitor plaza at an apron bearing of 262.1° true. The fitted apron clears the nearest PMTiles path by 1.21 m. Its retaining edge reaches the rendered canal surface. In the dated view the water mask follows the two dry apron outlines, with the rest of the canal and the path preserved. The exact capture day, original platform elevation and present exhibit condition remain unresolved.",
